NP.TXT:
In reply to a question put by the Court, theCommissionexplained that Articles 49 to 53 of the Act of Accession (Section 1 of Chapter 2 entitled
          Capital movements
          ) contained provisions authorizing the Hellenic Republic to defer the liberalization of capital movements until31 December 1985at the latest, by way of derogation from the provisions of the first and second directives for the implementation of Article 67 of the Treaty. The purpose of Article 52 was therefore to lay down the conditions under which the provisions concerning blocked funds would be applied during the transition period expiring on31 December 1985.
